    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1041 ;
    :rationaleText "This technique may be mitigated depending on where ingress and egress is tightly controlled. For example, the use network signatures such as IP addresses or domain names to identify traffic for specific adversary malware can be used to mitigate activity at the network level." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1042 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1048 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1048 ;
    :rationaleText "When outbound filtering is configured, a server firewall can block unauthorized protocols used to exfiltrate data. Effectiveness depends on whether egress rules are enforced rather than allowing unrestricted outbound traffic." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 931 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1048.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1048.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Outbound firewall restrictions can block unapproved encrypted non-C2 protocols or destinations used for exfiltration. The control is less effective when the traffic uses an explicitly permitted protocol and destination." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 932 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1048.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1048.002 ;
    :rationaleText "A managed egress policy can prevent servers from establishing unapproved asymmetric encrypted connections used to transfer data. This mitigation depends on restrictive outbound rules and destination controls." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 933 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1048.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1048.003 ;
    :rationaleText "A host firewall can block unauthorized outbound protocols and ports used for unencrypted data exfiltration. Exfiltration over an explicitly permitted service may remain possible." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 934 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1071 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1071 ;
    :rationaleText "Application-aware or restrictive outbound firewall rules can limit unauthorized HTTP, HTTPS, DNS, SMTP, and other application-layer communications used for command and control. A basic port-only policy provides limited protection when adversaries use permitted protocols." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 935 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1071.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1071.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Adversaries use web protocols to blend with normal traffic. A server firewall can partially restrict which destinations, ports, and web services a server may contact, though it will not stop all HTTP/S abuse. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1049 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1090 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1090 ;
    :rationaleText "Restricting outbound server connections can prevent malware from reaching unauthorized proxy infrastructure or accepting proxy traffic on unapproved ports. Proxy activity over approved channels may still succeed." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 936 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1090.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1090.003 ;
    :rationaleText "This technique may be lessened or mitigated though the use of firewall policy that constrains relay and redirect paths. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1046 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1095 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1095 ;
    :rationaleText "Host firewalls can restrict raw IP, ICMP, GRE, and other non-application-layer protocols used for command and control. The mitigation depends on denying protocols that the server does not explicitly require." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 937 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1105 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1105 ;
    :rationaleText "Restrictive outbound firewall rules can prevent a compromised server from downloading tools or payloads from unapproved external systems. The mapping is partial because transfers over approved destinations and protocols may still be possible." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 938 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1133 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1133 ;
    :rationaleText "A default-deny host firewall reduces the exposure of externally accessible remote services by permitting only explicitly authorized ports, protocols, and source systems." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 939 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1190 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1190 ;
    :rationaleText "A host firewall cannot remove vulnerabilities in a public-facing application, but it can ensure that only intended application ports are reachable and restrict access by source where operationally feasible. This reduces unnecessary exposure and possible exploitation paths." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 940 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1197 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
