    :sourceRecordNumber 1045 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1219 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1219 ;
    :rationaleText "Host firewall rules can block inbound or outbound communications associated with unauthorized remote access software. The firewall does not prevent the software from being installed or executed when it communicates over an allowed channel." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 943 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1537 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1537 ;
    :rationaleText "Egress filtering can restrict server connections to unauthorized cloud services or accounts, making cloud-based data transfer more difficult. The mitigation depends on destination-aware outbound controls." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 944 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1552.005 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1552.005 ;
    :rationaleText "ATT&CK mentions to limit access to the Instance Metadata API using a host-based firewall such as iptables. A properly configured Web Application Firewall (WAF) may help prevent external adversaries from exploiting Server-side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks that allow access to the Cloud Instance Metadata API." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1044 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1557.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1557.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Blocking unnecessary LLMNR, NBT-NS, mDNS, NetBIOS, and SMB traffic can reduce name-resolution poisoning and relay opportunities involving servers. Disabling the protocols and enforcing SMB signing remain stronger primary mitigations." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 945 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1557.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1557.002 ;
    :rationaleText "A host firewall may restrict follow-on connections created through ARP poisoning, but it has limited ability to prevent manipulation of Layer 2 address resolution itself. This is therefore a weak and environment-dependent mitigation." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 946 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1557.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1557.003 ;
    :rationaleText "A host firewall may limit some follow-on communications after a malicious DHCP configuration is accepted, but it does not directly prevent DHCP spoofing. Network access controls and DHCP protections are the primary mitigations." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 947 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1563.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1563.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Adversaries leverage RDP if it is reachable. Firewall rules are among the most direct ways to prevent unauthorized RDP reachability to servers. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1050 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1570 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1570 ;
    :rationaleText "Lateral tool transfers often rely on SMB, WinRM, SSH, or other network services that are directly governed by server firewall rules. Restricting those services to approved systems impedes common transfer channels." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 948 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1571 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1571 ;
    :rationaleText "A default-deny firewall blocks communication over arbitrary or non-standard ports unless they are explicitly permitted, directly limiting adversary use of unexpected ports." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 949 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1572 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1572 ;
    :rationaleText "Restricting permitted ports, protocols, and destinations can impede protocol tunneling from compromised servers. Tunnels carried inside an explicitly allowed protocol may still bypass simple port-based filtering." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 950 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1602.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1602.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Blocking unnecessary SNMP traffic and restricting authorized SNMP sources reduces the ability to query management information from servers or server-hosted management services. The applicability depends on whether the server exposes SNMP." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 951 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1686 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1686 ;
    :rationaleText "Adversaries may disable or alter host firewall configurations to expose services or enable unrestricted network communication, directly undermining the safeguard. Implementing and actively managing the firewall establishes the required configuration and supports identifying or correcting unauthorized changes." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 952 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1686.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1686.001 ;
    :rationaleText "This sub-technique concerns changes to cloud firewall rules or security groups rather than a host-based firewall installed on a server. The relationship to Safeguard 4.4 is therefore indirect and primarily relevant where server firewall management also encompasses associated cloud firewall controls." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 953 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1686.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1686.002 ;
    :rationaleText "This sub-technique targets firewalls implemented on network infrastructure rather than host-based firewalls on servers. Its relationship to Safeguard 4.4 is weak and applies only where the server firewall management process also governs supporting network firewall policy." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 954 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.4_T1686.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1686.003 ;
    :rationaleText "This sub-technique explicitly covers disabling or modifying the Windows host firewall, including changing profiles or rules to expose services or permit command-and-control traffic. Implementing and managing the required firewall configuration helps identify, prevent, or reverse unauthorized changes." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 955 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1021 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021 ;
    :rationaleText "A default-deny endpoint firewall directly restricts unsolicited remote-service connections and permits access only through explicitly approved services, ports, and management paths." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 868 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1021.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Restricting TCP 3389 to approved management sources directly prevents unauthorized RDP connections and reduces RDP-based lateral movement." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 869 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1021.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Blocking or tightly restricting TCP 445 and 139 directly impedes access to administrative shares and other SMB-based lateral movement paths." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 870 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1021.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.003 ;
    :rationaleText "A firewall can restrict DCOM by controlling RPC endpoint mapper traffic and dynamic RPC ports. The relationship is direct, but implementation is more complex than filtering a single fixed port." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 876 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1021.004 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.004 ;
    :rationaleText "A default-deny firewall can block inbound SSH or restrict TCP 22 to approved management systems, directly limiting remote access to SSH-enabled end-user devices." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 871 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1021.005 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.005 ;
    :rationaleText "VNC requires an accessible listener, commonly on TCP 5900 and related ports. Blocking those ports unless specifically authorized directly prevents unauthorized VNC access." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 872 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1021.006 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
