    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1571 ;
    :rationaleText "Default-deny rules directly block arbitrary and unexpected ports unless they have been explicitly approved, limiting adversary communications over non-standard ports." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 875 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.5_T1572 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1572 ;
    :rationaleText "Limiting approved ports, protocols, services, and destinations can prevent many unauthorized tunnels. Tunnels encapsulated within an approved HTTPS, DNS, or SSH connection may still succeed." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 897 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021 ;
    :rationaleText "Securely managing which remote services are permitted and requiring authenticated encrypted protocols reduces exposed administrative paths. The safeguard does not independently prevent adversaries from using valid credentials through an approved service." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 831 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure RDP configuration, gateways, TLS, and restricted administrative access reduce interception and direct exposure. RDP remains usable by an adversary who possesses authorized credentials or an active session." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 832 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure management can disable unnecessary administrative shares and require modern SMB signing or encryption where remote administration is needed. It does not fully prevent abuse of an authorized SMB management path." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 833 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.003 ;
    :rationaleText "Securely managing DCOM availability and restricting it to approved administrative workflows reduces remote abuse. DCOM does not have a simple SSH or HTTPS replacement, so effectiveness depends on disabling or tightly constraining it." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 834 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.004 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.004 ;
    :rationaleText "SSH protects administrative credentials and commands from plaintext interception and should replace Telnet. It does not prevent an adversary with valid credentials or an unauthorized SSH key from using the service." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 835 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.005 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.005 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure management can prohibit unencrypted VNC deployments or require encrypted tunnels and approved administrative tooling. The relationship is partial because some VNC implementations or tunnels remain accessible with valid credentials." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 836 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.006 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.006 ;
    :rationaleText "Requiring WinRM over HTTPS rather than unencrypted HTTP protects management credentials and commands in transit. Authorized-account abuse remains possible through the secured channel." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 837 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.007 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.007 ;
    :rationaleText "Securing cloud administrative consoles and APIs, using controlled automation, and managing resources through version-controlled Infrastructure-as-Code reduces ad hoc and insecure administration. It does not prevent malicious activity performed through a compromised authorized cloud account." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 838 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1021.008 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1021.008 ;
    :rationaleText "Approved and securely configured cloud-native VM connection methods reduce exposure from direct or insecure management services. Cloud control-plane access may bypass the guest operating system's network controls, so identity and cloud policy protections are also required." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 839 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1040 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1040 ;
    :rationaleText "Replacing plaintext administrative protocols such as Telnet and HTTP with SSH and HTTPS prevents captured management traffic from directly exposing credentials, commands, and configuration data. Encryption does not prevent packet capture, but it materially reduces the value of the captured traffic." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 819 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1059.008 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1059.008 ;
    :rationaleText "Requiring SSH rather than Telnet protects command-line interface credentials and commands in transit and reduces interception or manipulation. Once an adversary has authorized administrative access, the encrypted CLI still permits malicious commands." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 840 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1072 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1072 ;
    :rationaleText "Safeguard 4.6 directly concerns securely managing software and configuration-management platforms, including tools integrated with CI/CD systems. Restricting administrative access and managing deployment configuration through controlled, versioned mechanisms reduces unauthorized use of these platforms for execution and lateral movement." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 820 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1090.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1090.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure SSH configuration can disable unnecessary forwarding and proxy features, reducing the ability to turn a managed asset into a pivot. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 862 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1098.004 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1098.004 ;
    :rationaleText "Version-controlled SSH configuration and managed deployment of approved keys can prevent or identify unauthorized additions to authorized_keys. File permissions and privileged access controls are still needed to prevent local modification." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 843 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1133 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1133 ;
    :rationaleText "Requiring secure protocols and centrally managed administrative access reduces risk from externally accessible management services. Additional protections such as multi-factor authentication, gateways, and network restrictions remain necessary." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 841 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1190 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1190 ;
    :rationaleText "Administrative web interfaces should use HTTPS and should not be exposed through unnecessary plaintext or legacy services. HTTPS does not remediate an application vulnerability, so this mitigation primarily reduces unnecessary exposure and traffic manipulation." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 842 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1210 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1210 ;
    :rationaleText "Disabling obsolete management protocols and securely configuring required administrative services reduces the number of remotely reachable and vulnerable services. The safeguard does not patch vulnerabilities, but it directly removes insecure management paths that could be exploited." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 821 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1213.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1213.003 ;
    :rationaleText "Infrastructure-as-Code repositories may reveal infrastructure topology, administrative endpoints, configuration, and embedded credentials. Secure repository administration and keeping secrets outside version control reduce the value and accessibility of these repositories." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 844 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1219 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1219 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure software management can limit administration to approved and securely configured remote-access products. The safeguard does not prevent an approved tool or account from being abused by an adversary." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 845 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1219.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1219.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Securely managing development tools can disable unnecessary tunneling functions and restrict approved remote-development services. Legitimate HTTPS or SSH development channels may still be abused." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 846 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1219.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1219.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Organizations can centrally approve, configure, and secure remote-support software while removing unauthorized products. An adversary may still misuse an approved product or compromised support account." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 847 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1484 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1484 ;
    :rationaleText "Version-controlled domain or tenant configuration can make unauthorized policy changes visible and allow restoration to approved state. Many identity policies are still managed directly through consoles or APIs rather than Infrastructure-as-Code." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 864 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1484.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1484.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Managing Group Policy definitions through controlled configuration processes can identify or reverse unauthorized changes. Version control does not prevent direct modification by an account that retains write access to the policy." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 865 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1552.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1552.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Infrastructure code, configuration files, deployment manifests, and automation scripts frequently create a risk of embedded passwords or tokens. Secure management should keep credentials out of source-controlled configuration and use protected secret stores or runtime injection." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 848 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1552.004 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1552.004 ;
    :rationaleText "SSH administration depends on protecting private keys and preventing them from being embedded in repositories or widely distributed. Managed key storage, permissions, and rotation reduce the likelihood that stolen keys can be used for administration." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 849 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1552.007 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1552.007 ;
    :rationaleText "Disabling unauthenticated Docker and Kubernetes API access and requiring secured channels such as SSH or TLS directly reduces unauthorized access to container-management interfaces. This closely matches the safeguard's requirement to access administrative interfaces through secure protocols." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 822 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1557 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1557 ;
    :rationaleText "Authenticated encryption through SSH, HTTPS, and TLS limits an adversary's ability to read or alter administrative traffic even after obtaining a network interception position. Certificate and SSH host-key validation remain essential to the effectiveness of the mitigation." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 823 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1557.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1557.001 ;
    :rationaleText "SSH host-key validation, HTTPS certificate validation, SMB signing, and encrypted management channels reduce the ability to capture or relay administrative authentication. Disabling LLMNR, NBT-NS, and unnecessary SMB remains an important complementary control." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 854 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1557.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1557.002 ;
    :rationaleText "An adversary may still redirect management traffic through ARP poisoning, but properly validated SSH and HTTPS sessions protect the confidentiality and integrity of that traffic. The safeguard does not prevent the underlying ARP manipulation." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 855 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1557.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1557.003 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure protocols reduce credential theft and command manipulation even if DHCP spoofing redirects traffic. DHCP snooping and network-level controls are still required to prevent the spoofing behavior itself." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 856 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1563 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1563 ;
    :rationaleText "Securely configuring remote services can reduce unnecessary sessions and restrict features that facilitate hijacking. Encryption does not prevent an adversary already executing on a system from taking control of an existing session." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 859 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1563.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1563.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Disabling SSH agent forwarding and tightly managing SSH configuration reduces some hijacking paths. It does not prevent local theft or reuse of an established SSH socket or session." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 860 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1563.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1563.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure RDP gateways and restricted administration reduce access to RDP sessions. They do not prevent a locally privileged adversary from taking control of an existing session." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 861 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1565 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1565 ;
    :rationaleText "Version-controlled configuration and authenticated encrypted management channels reduce unauthorized or undetected changes to enterprise configuration. The safeguard does not protect every type of business or application data." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 857 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1565.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1565.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Version-controlled Infrastructure-as-Code provides history, review, comparison, and restoration for managed configurations, reducing the persistence of unauthorized configuration changes. This applies only where the affected configuration is actually managed as code." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 858 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1565.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1565.002 ;
    :rationaleText "SSH and HTTPS provide confidentiality and integrity protection for management commands and configuration data in transit. This makes undetected modification of administrative traffic substantially more difficult." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 824 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1572 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1572 ;
    :rationaleText "Securely configuring SSH, VPN, and administrative tools can disable unnecessary port forwarding and tunneling functions. The safeguard does not prevent tunneling through an otherwise approved secure protocol when that capability is operationally required." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 863 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1578 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1578 ;
    :rationaleText "Version-controlled Infrastructure-as-Code can define expected compute infrastructure and identify or reverse out-of-band changes. An adversary with sufficient cloud permissions may still modify resources directly." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 866 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1578.005 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1578.005 ;
    :rationaleText "Infrastructure-as-Code provides an approved baseline for quotas, instance settings, and compute configurations, allowing unauthorized drift to be identified or corrected." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 867 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1602 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1602 ;
    :rationaleText "Secure management protocols, authenticated access, and controlled configuration repositories directly reduce unauthorized collection of device and infrastructure configuration. Version-controlled Infrastructure-as-Code can also reduce the need to retrieve configurations through insecure management interfaces." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 825 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1602.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1602.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Migrating from insecure SNMP versions to SNMPv3 with authentication and privacy protection directly reduces unauthorized MIB collection. Restricting management access to approved systems further limits successful enumeration." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 826 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1602.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1602.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Using SSH, HTTPS, SNMPv3, and securely managed configuration repositories reduces exposure of network-device configurations and embedded credentials. Insecure services such as Telnet, HTTP, TFTP, or legacy management protocols create substantially greater collection risk." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 827 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-4.6_T1609 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-4 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-4.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1609 ;
    :rationaleText "Restricting Docker and Kubernetes administration to authenticated TLS, SSH, local sockets, or other secured management channels directly reduces unauthorized remote container commands. Version-controlled manifests and Infrastructure-as-Code also reduce unreviewed administrative changes." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 828 .

