    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1048.001 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering can block resolution of a known malicious exfiltration destination regardless of whether the transmitted data is encrypted." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 738 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1048.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1048.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Blocking a known malicious destination domain may interrupt an asymmetric encrypted exfiltration channel. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 739 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1048.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1048.003 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS can carry encoded exfiltrated data over an unencrypted non-command-and-control protocol. Blocking resolution of an adversary-controlled domain can interrupt DNS-based exfiltration, although newly registered or uncategorized domains may initially be allowed." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 732 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1071 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1071 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering directly affects DNS and can also prevent connections to malicious domains used for web-based application-layer command and control. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 729 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1071.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1071.001 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering can prevent HTTP, HTTPS, and WebSocket command-and-control connections when the destination domain has been classified as malicious. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 730 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1071.004 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1071.004 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering can prevent resolution of known malicious domains used for DNS-based command and control and can sinkhole requests before an endpoint reaches adversary infrastructure." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 725 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1105 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1105 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering can prevent a compromised endpoint from resolving known malicious domains used to host tools or secondary payloads. Transfers over direct IP addresses, approved cloud services, compromised legitimate domains, or uncategorized domains may still succeed." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 733 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1189 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1189 ;
    :rationaleText "Blocking known malicious or compromised domains prevents browsers from reaching websites used to exploit users or deliver malicious content. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 726 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1204.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1204.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Even when a user clicks a malicious link, DNS filtering can prevent successful navigation when the destination domain is known to be malicious. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 728 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1566 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering materially mitigates phishing that directs users to malicious domains. It does not mitigate phishing attachments, voice phishing, or messages that do not require visiting a domain." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 734 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1566.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566.002 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering can block the destination of a malicious link delivered through email before the user reaches a credential-harvesting page, exploit site, or malware download. Newly registered, compromised, or uncategorized domains may initially evade filtering." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 727 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1568 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1568 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS sinkholing and reputation-based filtering can prevent resolution of identified dynamic-DNS and generated domains used to reestablish command and control." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 736 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1568.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1568.002 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering services may block or sinkhole known and predicted algorithmically generated domains, for example those that have high entropy in the name. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 737 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.2_T1572 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.2 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1572 ;
    :rationaleText "DNS filtering can block tunnels that depend on resolving known malicious domains, including some DNS and web-based tunnels. Tunnels using direct IP addresses, trusted domains, or infrastructure not yet classified as malicious may still succeed." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 735 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1102 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1102 ;
    :rationaleText "CIS 9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content in the first place. It does this by requiring updated network-based URL filtering across all enterprise assets, using methods such as category-based filtering, reputation-based filtering, and block lists. In practice, this means enforcing controls that restrict access to unsafe websites, malicious downloads, risky scripts, and unauthorized browser extensions, reducing the risk of phishing, exploitation, and malware delivery. If 9.3 implementation includes certain risky or suspicious web-services used broadly enough to block unauthorized services, then this technique is applicable. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1141 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1102.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1102.001 ;
    :rationaleText """CIS 9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content. If 9.3 implementation blocks unapproved social media, code repositories, paste sites, and similar web services across enterprise HTTP/S traffic, this becomes defensible. Adversaries may post content, known as a dead drop resolver, on Web services with embedded (and often obfuscated/encoded) domains or IP addresses. Once infected, victims will reach out to and be redirected by these resolvers.

""" ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1140 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1102.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1102.002 ;
    :rationaleText "If 9.3 implementation includes outbound web-service use broadly enough to block unauthorized services and risky websites, then this technique is applicable. ATT&CK describes two-way C2 via legitimate web services and again points to web proxies and blocking unauthorized external services as mitigation." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1138 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1102.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1102.003 ;
    :rationaleText """Popular websites and social media acting as a mechanism for C2 may give a significant amount of cover due to the likelihood that hosts within a network are already communicating with them prior to a compromise. Using common services, such as those offered by Google or Twitter, makes it easier for adversaries to hide in expected noise.

9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content.  If 9.3 implementation includes outbound web-services used broadly enough to block unauthorized services and restrict access to unsafe websites, then this technique is defensible. """ ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1139 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1105 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1105 ;
    :rationaleText """9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content by requiring updated network-based URL filtering across all enterprise assets, using methods such as category-based filtering, reputation-based filtering, and block lists. 

In practice, this means enforcing controls that restrict access to unsafe websites, malicious downloads, risky scripts, and unauthorized browser extensions, reducing the risk of phishing, exploitation, and malware delivery. If 9.3 implementation blocks outbound traffic from machines to unapproved external destinations. Restricting access to known, trusted IP addresses and protocols can prevent attackers from downloading malicious tools or payloads onto compromised servers after gaining initial access. """ ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1134 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1189 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1189 ;
    :rationaleText "CIS 9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content in the first place. It does this by requiring updated network-based URL filtering across all enterprise assets, using methods such as category-based filtering, reputation-based filtering, and block lists. In practice, this means enforcing controls that restrict access to unsafe websites, malicious downloads, risky scripts, and unauthorized browser extensions, reducing the risk of phishing, exploitation, and malware delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1133 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1204 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1204 ;
    :rationaleText "9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content in the first place. It does this by requiring updated network-based URL filtering across all enterprise assets, using methods such as category-based filtering, reputation-based filtering, and block lists. In practice, this means enforcing controls that restrict access to unsafe websites, malicious downloads, risky scripts, and unauthorized browser extensions, reducing the risk of phishing, exploitation, and malware delivery. If 9.3 is implemented as a secure web gateway or proxy that can stop the post-click fetch/download, then this technique is applicable. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1142 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1204.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1204.001 ;
    :rationaleText " 9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content in the first place. It does this by requiring updated network-based URL filtering across all enterprise assets, using methods such as category-based filtering, reputation-based filtering, and block lists. In practice, this means enforcing controls that restrict access to unsafe websites, malicious downloads, risky scripts, and unauthorized browser extensions, reducing the risk of phishing, exploitation, and malware delivery. If 9.3 is implemented as a secure web gateway or proxy that can stop the post-click fetch/download, then this technique is applicable. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1143 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1566 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
