    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566 ;
    :rationaleText "9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content in the first place. It does this by requiring updated network-based URL filtering across all enterprise assets, using methods such as category-based filtering, reputation-based filtering, and block lists. In practice, this means enforcing controls that restrict access to unsafe websites, malicious downloads, risky scripts, and unauthorized browser extensions, reducing the risk of phishing, exploitation, and malware delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1145 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1566.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566.002 ;
    :rationaleText "9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content in the first place. It does this by requiring updated network-based URL filtering across all enterprise assets, using methods such as category-based filtering, reputation-based filtering, and block lists. In practice, this means enforcing controls that restrict access to unsafe websites, malicious downloads, risky scripts, and unauthorized browser extensions, reducing the risk of phishing, exploitation, and malware delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1144 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1567.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1567.002 ;
    :rationaleText "9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved sites. If 9.3 implementation blocks the URLs of unauthorized cloud storage services that are not approved by the organization then this technique is defensible. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1136 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1567.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1567.003 ;
    :rationaleText "9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content in the first place. Adversaries may exfiltrate data to text storage sites instead of their primary command and control channel. If 9.3 implementation blocks unauthorized text storage sites, the technique is defensible. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1135 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.3_T1593.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.3 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1593.003 ;
    :rationaleText "9.3 helps prevent link-based and web-based initial access by stopping users from reaching malicious or unapproved content. If 9.3 implementation blocks unapproved code repositories and repository APIs, this is applicable." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1137 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1137 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1137 ;
    :rationaleText "Restricting email-client add-ins mitigates the add-in portion of this parent technique. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 720 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1137.006 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1137.006 ;
    :rationaleText "Disabling unauthorized Outlook add-ins prevents those add-ins from automatically loading code when the email client starts. This directly reduces persistence through email-client add-on functionality." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 718 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1176 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1176 ;
    :rationaleText "This technique includes browser extensions, which are directly addressed by the safeguard. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 719 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1176.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1176.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Browser extension allowlists, denylists, installation restrictions, and removal of unauthorized extensions directly prevent malicious browser extensions from establishing persistence or abusing inherited browser permissions." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 717 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1189 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1189 ;
    :rationaleText "Removing unnecessary or vulnerable browser plug-ins reduces components that a malicious website can enumerate and exploit during a drive-by attack. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 723 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1203 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1203 ;
    :rationaleText "Uninstalling unnecessary browser or email-client plug-ins removes potential client-side exploitation targets. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 724 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1539 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1539 ;
    :rationaleText "Malicious browser extensions may access browser cookies and session information. Restricting extensions removes one important cookie-theft path." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 721 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.4_T1555.003 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.4 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1555.003 ;
    :rationaleText "Malicious extensions may access credentials stored in browsers. Extension restrictions reduce that attack surface, but malware already executing with access to the browser profile may still extract stored credentials." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 722 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.5_T1566 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566 ;
    :rationaleText "DMARC may materially reduces phishing campaigns that rely on spoofed or unauthenticated sender domains." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 965 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.5_T1566.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566.001 ;
    :rationaleText "DMARC may materially reduces phishing campaigns that rely on spoofed or unauthenticated sender domains. DMARC may reduce attachment-led spearphishing when the campaign depends on spoofed sender trust and domain authentication failure. It does not inspect the attachment itself though. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 964 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.5_T1566.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566.002 ;
    :rationaleText "DMARC may materially reduces phishing campaigns that rely on spoofed or unauthenticated sender domains. DMARC may reduce link-led spearphishing at the sender-authentication and mail acceptance time. It does not inspect the attachment itself though. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 963 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.5_T1667 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1667 ;
    :rationaleText "ATT&CK explicitly discusses DMARC, SPF, and DKIM on the Email bombing technique page, including how enabling these mechanisms within an organization (through policies such as DMARC) may enable recipients (intra-org and cross domain) to perform similar message filtering and validation to mitigate this technique. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 959 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.5_T1684 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1684 ;
    :rationaleText "Social engineering is broadly defined as influencing users into actions while minimizing technical indicators, DMARC can be a meaningful control against the email-spoofing branch of this broader technique. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 966 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.5_T1684.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1684.001 ;
    :rationaleText "DMARC may not stop all impersonation, but it reduces a major subset where trust is created through control of the visible sender identity and aligned sending domain." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 967 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.5_T1684.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.5 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1684.002 ;
    :rationaleText "ATT&CK explicitly discusses DMARC, SPF, and DKIM on the Email Spoofing technique page, including how weak or absent DMARC leaves spoofed messages deliverable and how DMARC-enabled filtering mitigates the behavior" ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 968 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1027.006 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.006 ;
    :rationaleText "For this technique, adversaries may smuggle data and files past content filters by hiding malicious payloads inside of seemingly benign HTML files. If the implementation for 9.3 can mitigate this technique if it disallows .html, .htm, .hta, and similar active content files as email attachments on the block list. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1057 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1027.009 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.009 ;
    :rationaleText "File blocking mitigates embedded payloads by completely stripping high-risk file types at the perimeter, denying attackers the ability to deliver the initial malicious file or its nested, obfuscated components. Attackers frequently embed malicious scripts (e.g., .js, .vbs) inside legitimate document formats (e.g., PDFs, Word docs). By blocking macro-enabled or script-based file types, gateways prevent these malicious combinations from ever reaching the user's inbox" ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1055 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1027.012 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.012 ;
    :rationaleText "LNK files are used as phishing payloads and when a user invokes them they can download or execute additional payloads. If .lnk objects are blocked at the email boundary then it can mitigate the delivery of this technique. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1056 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1027.015 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.015 ;
    :rationaleText "9.6 can prevent this type of technique if it blocks RAR, 7z, and other known unauthorized self-extracting archive types from specific machines. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1058 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1059.005 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1059.005 ;
    :rationaleText "Adversaries may use VB payloads to execute malicious commands. Common malicious usage includes automating execution of behaviors with VBScript or embedding VBA content into spearphishing Attachment payloads. If .VB objects are blocked at the email boundary then it can mitigate the spearphishing delivery of this technique. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1052 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1137.006 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1137.006 ;
    :rationaleText "dversaries often weaponize Office add-ins (e.g., Excel .xll files or Outlook .wll / .ecf extensions) by sending them via phishing campaigns. Blocking these file types at the email boundary prevents the initial execution and subsequent installation of malicious persistence mechanisms. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1054 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1204 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1204 ;
    :rationaleText "9.6 enforcement can reduce user exposure by removing risky files upstream at the point of email delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1060 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1204.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1204.002 ;
    :rationaleText "9.6 enforcement can reduce user exposure by removing risky files upstream at the point of email delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1059 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1218.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1218.001 ;
    :rationaleText "A custom CHM file containing embedded payloads could be delivered to a victim through email then triggered by User Execution If those custom CHM files are blocked at the email boundary, then it can mitigate the delivery of this technique. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1053 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1553.005 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1553.005 ;
    :rationaleText "Adversaries may abuse container files such as compressed/archive (.arj, .gzip) and/or disk image (.iso, .vhd) file formats to deliver malicious payloads. The execution prevention mitigation mentions the use of blocking container file types at web and/or email gateways which could apply to the implementation of this safeguard." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1051 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1566 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566 ;
    :rationaleText "9.6 is a preventive email-gateway control that blocks disallowed attachment types before delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1062 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.6_T1566.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.6 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566.001 ;
    :rationaleText "9.6 is a preventive email-gateway control that blocks disallowed attachment types before delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 1061 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027 ;
    :rationaleText "Email anti-malware can use static, heuristic, and behavioral analysis to identify obfuscated files before delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 703 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Heuristic scanning and sandbox detonation can identify packed executables attached to messages, even when packing changes their static signature. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 704 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027.006 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.006 ;
    :rationaleText "A sandbox capable of executing active HTML attachments may detect JavaScript that reconstructs and writes a malicious payload to disk. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 705 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027.009 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.009 ;
    :rationaleText "Attachment scanners and sandboxes can identify malicious payloads hidden within documents, scripts, executables, or other carrier files." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 706 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027.012 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.012 ;
    :rationaleText "Email scanning can identify suspicious LNK attachments and inspect icon-location or target fields that reference remote payloads." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 699 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027.013 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.013 ;
    :rationaleText "Anti-malware can identify encoded or high-entropy attachments and may block encrypted archives that cannot be inspected. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 707 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027.015 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.015 ;
    :rationaleText "Email anti-malware capable of recursively unpacking ZIP, RAR, 7z, self-extracting archives, and nested archives can identify malicious files before delivery. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 708 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1027.017 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1027.017 ;
    :rationaleText "A sandbox that renders SVG attachments and executes their embedded scripts may identify payload construction or malicious follow-on behavior. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 709 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1036 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1036 ;
    :rationaleText "Anti-malware analysis can identify malicious attachments whose content, signature, or behavior conflicts with their apparent name or file type. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 710 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1036.007 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1036.007 ;
    :rationaleText "Email gateways can inspect the complete filename and actual file type rather than relying on the first visible extension, allowing attachments such as invoice.pdf.exe or report.pdf.lnk to be blocked." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 711 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1036.008 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1036.008 ;
    :rationaleText "Anti-malware scanners can compare file headers, MIME types, extensions, and content to detect attachments disguised as benign file formats." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 700 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1059 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1059 ;
    :rationaleText "Email anti-malware can block suspicious script attachments before they reach an interpreter. Most command and scripting activity occurs after compromise or through channels unrelated to email." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 713 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1059.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1059.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Email scanning or sandboxing may identify PowerShell script attachments or documents that launch PowerShell. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 714 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1059.005 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1059.005 ;
    :rationaleText "Email anti-malware and sandboxing can analyze Visual Basic scripts and macro-enabled attachments and quarantine files that exhibit malicious behavior. This does not prevent Visual Basic abuse originating outside email." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 712 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1059.006 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1059.006 ;
    :rationaleText "Email anti-malware may quarantine malicious Python scripts or packed Python payloads sent specifically as email attachments. Python activity originating from installed tools or post-compromise execution remains unaffected." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 715 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1059.007 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1059.007 ;
    :rationaleText "A sandbox may execute JavaScript, JScript, HTA, HTML, or SVG attachments and identify malicious file creation or process execution. Depends on the email security product supporting active-content detonation." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 716 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1203 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1203 ;
    :rationaleText "Email sandboxing can detonate weaponized Office documents, PDFs, archives, and other attachments to identify exploit behavior before delivery." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 697 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1204 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1204 ;
    :rationaleText "Blocking malicious attachments prevents one major form of user execution. " ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 702 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1204.002 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1204.002 ;
    :rationaleText "Removing a malicious attachment before delivery prevents the user from opening the file and initiating its execution chain. The safeguard is limited to malicious files delivered through the protected email environment." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 696 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1221 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1221 ;
    :rationaleText "Email detonation chambers can open suspicious documents and observe attempts to retrieve or execute remote templates and payloads before the message reaches the recipient." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 698 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1566 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566 ;
    :rationaleText "Email-server anti-malware directly addresses malicious attachments." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 701 .

data:cisassertion_CIS-9.7_T1566.001 a :MitigatesAssertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom data:cisDataset ;
    :assertedMappingType :mappingType_mitigates ;
    :assertedStatus :mappingStatus_complete ;
    :assertsCapabilityGroup data:cisgroup_CIS-9 ;
    :assertsControl data:cis_CIS-9.7 ;
    :assertsTechnique data:technique_T1566.001 ;
    :rationaleText "Email-server attachment scanning and sandboxing can identify, quarantine, or remove malicious attachments before they reach the recipient." ;
    :sourceRecordNumber 695 .

